# BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile in place of a root .dockerignore, so
# this narrows the adapter's build context without changing what any other image sees. Only what the
# Dockerfile copies is sent: no node_modules, no .git, no local secrets.
*
!package.json
!src
!public
!adapters/node
# THE RE-INCLUDE ABOVE TAKES EVERYTHING UNDER adapters/node, the operator's .env with it, and the
# Dockerfile copies that directory whole. A review (2026-11-25) caught it: docs/SELF-HOSTING.md has the
# operator write RESOLVER_SECRET and any *_ACCOUNTS cookie jars into adapters/node/.env, so every image
# built that way carried live secrets in a layer, one `docker push` from public. The last matching rule
# wins, so these exclusions must stay BELOW the re-include. compose reads the file at run time
# (env_file); the image never needs it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
adapters/node/data
adapters/node/media
